This project includes or derives from the following.

renfe-flipdot-re
  https://github.com/oierlauzi/renfe-flipdot-re  (MIT, same author)
  The first replica, its artwork geometry and the mitren.app client were
  ported from its web replica. The 5x7 character set in
  src/lib/hardware/fonts/telenorma-5x7.ts was read out of the ROM of a PAGE
  Ibérica PI-T100-M (Telenorma firmware AK0052.139U1) by that project; the
  glyph shapes are reproduced for interoperability research and
  preservation.

¿Dónde está mi tren? (dondeestamitren, mitren.app)
  https://github.com/jotaelediaz/dondeestamitren  (Apache-2.0)
  src/lib/sources/mitren/stations.data.json is generated from the station
  data that project ships, by tools/build_stations.py: the networks of
  Renfe Cercanías, of Euskotren and of Metro Bilbao. The live source
  reads the public WebSocket of its deployment at https://mitren.app/.

Adif and Renfe
  The adif source reads the boards ADIF publishes for its stations' screens
  at https://info.adif.es/. src/lib/sources/adif/stations.data.json is
  generated by tools/build_adif_stations.py from Renfe's register of stations
  (https://data.renfe.com/dataset/estaciones-listado-completo, CC BY 4.0),
  with the names ADIF's boards print and mitren.app's list of Cercanías
  stations. tests/fixtures/adif/ holds boards recorded from info.adif.es.

Photographs
